cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its findings, please cite it as below."
title: "neural-cdma: Engineered CDMA Superposition in Pretrained LLMs — channel physics (Paper B) and activation-side session tagging for audit logs (Paper A)"
abstract: >-
  Two companion papers built from the result files in this repository. Paper B
  (channel physics): engineered CDMA superposition in off-the-shelf pretrained
  transformers survives only in the linear channel or with a trained
  de-multiplexer; five untrained non-linear readouts collapse it; causal language
  caps the multiplexing capacity at K_cap = 2 and per-token surprise predicts
  multiplexability. Paper A (audit-log tag): a key-conditioned session tag in the
  residual stream, verifiable by paired replay of logged activations under a
  commit-then-verify threat model, with per-session statistics on Qwen2.5-0.5B,
  1.5B and 7B; it does not prove model execution, is not blind-decodable and is
  not a text watermark. Version 1 claims of legal non-repudiation are withdrawn.
